.git
.github
.claude
# …except the coordinator's skills. `.claude/skills/next-issue` holds the
# preflight decision table next to the procedure it describes, and
# `packages/cli/test/preflight-tier.test.ts` reads both to prove they agree — a
# review image without them can only skip that suite. Everything else under
# `.claude` (worktrees, local settings) stays out.
!.claude/skills
!.claude/skills/**
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
data
**/data
# A root-anchored pattern matches only the repository root, so every one of
# these gets a `**/` twin: a database or a derived config one directory down is
# exactly the file that must not reach a public image.
*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
**/*.sqlite-*
*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3
*.db
**/*.db
# …except two tracked fixtures, which are test data and nobody's corpus.
# `mise run review` runs the suites inside the image, and without these the
# hub's and the MCP server's SQLite tests have nothing to open.
!packages/hub/test/fixtures/extension-sqlite.sqlite
!packages/mcp-server/test/fixtures/better-sqlite3.sqlite
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
test-results
playwright-report
.DS_Store
.vite

# A developer's derived mise config carries HUB_AUTH_TOKEN. It is gitignored, so
# `mise run review` (which builds from `git archive`) never sees it — but a plain
# `docker build` from a working checkout would otherwise bake the signing secret
# into an image that is published publicly. Both spellings, at every depth.
mise.local.toml
**/mise.local.toml
.mise.local.toml
**/.mise.local.toml
